Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and potential usage  
• PUBLICATIONS."cpc": contains CPC classification codes for each patent publication; needed to extract the first CPC code  
• PUBLICATIONS."filing_date": numeric filing date; filter to keep only records with a valid (non‑null, non‑zero) filing date  
• PUBLICATIONS."application_number": text; filter out records where this field is empty or null  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": can be shown for easy inspection of sample records  
• PUBLICATIONS."family_id": lets us aggregate filings that belong to the same patent family if desired  
• PUBLICATIONS."country_code", "kind_code", "application_kind": optional for additional filtering / inspection  
• CPC_DEFINITION."symbol": the CPC code (at any hierarchical level) – join key to PUBLICATIONS."cpc"  
• CPC_DEFINITION."titleFull": full textual title of the CPC technology area – returned in reports  
• CPC_DEFINITION."level": hierarchy depth; use `WHERE "level" = 5` to keep groups at level 5  
Conditions likely to be used  
• PUBLICATIONS."filing_date" IS NOT NULL AND "filing_date" > 0  
• PUBLICATIONS."application_number" IS NOT NULL AND "application_number" <> ''  
• After flattening PUBLICATIONS."cpc", keep only the first element (earliest position) per publication  
• Join CPC_DEFINITION ON the CPC symbol, then filter CPC_DEFINITION."level" = 5  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 rows each) that gradually move from very simple inspection to more complex aggregations.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a few raw publication records to understand key columns.
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "application_number",
  "filing_date",
  "cpc"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Inspect records that definitely have a filing date and application number.
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "application_number",
  "filing_date",
  "cpc"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "filing_date" IS NOT NULL
  AND "filing_date" > 0
  AND "application_number" IS NOT NULL
  AND "application_number" <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Flatten the CPC array to look at every individual CPC code attached to a publication.
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  p."filing_date",
  f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS "cpc_symbol",
  f.value:"title"::STRING  AS "cpc_title"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS AS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
WHERE p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
  AND p."filing_date" > 0
  AND p."application_number" IS NOT NULL
  AND p."application_number" <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Retrieve only the FIRST CPC code per publication (position = 0 in FLATTEN).
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  p."filing_date",
  f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS "first_cpc"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS AS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
WHERE f."index" = 0                -- first item in the array
  AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
  AND p."filing_date" > 0
  AND p."application_number" IS NOT NULL
  AND p."application_number" <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Join the first CPC symbol to the CPC_DEFINITION table to bring the full CPC title.
SELECT
  fpub."first_cpc"  AS "cpc_symbol",
  cd."titleFull"    AS "cpc_title",
  cd."level"
FROM (
  SELECT 
    f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS "first_cpc"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
  WHERE f."index" = 0
    AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
    AND p."filing_date" > 0
    AND p."application_number" IS NOT NULL
    AND p."application_number" <> ''
  LIMIT 200
) AS fpub
LEFT JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
  ON cd."symbol" = fpub."first_cpc"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Inspect only CPC definitions at hierarchy level 5.
SELECT 
  "symbol",
  "titleFull",
  "level"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION
WHERE "level" = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count how many filings (first‑CPC only) each CPC level‑5 group received per calendar year.
SELECT
  YEAR(TO_DATE("filing_date"::STRING, 'YYYYMMDD')) AS "year",
  cd."symbol"                                      AS "cpc_symbol",
  cd."titleFull"                                   AS "cpc_title",
  COUNT(*)                                         AS "filing_count"
FROM (
  SELECT 
    p."filing_date",
    f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS "first_cpc"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
  WHERE f."index" = 0
    AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
    AND p."filing_date" > 0
    AND p."application_number" IS NOT NULL
    AND p."application_number" <> ''
) pub
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
  ON cd."symbol" = pub."first_cpc"
WHERE cd."level" = 5
GROUP BY 1,2,3
ORDER BY 1,4 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Produce a running total of filings per CPC group to prepare for moving‑average tests.
SELECT
  cd."symbol"                                  AS "cpc_symbol",
  YEAR(TO_DATE("filing_date"::STRING, 'YYYYMMDD')) AS "year",
  COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY cd."symbol"
                 ORDER BY YEAR(TO_DATE("filing_date"::STRING, 'YYYYMMDD'))) AS "cumulative_filings"
FROM (
  SELECT 
    p."filing_date",
    f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS "first_cpc"
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
  WHERE f."index" = 0
    AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
    AND p."filing_date" > 0
    AND p."application_number" IS NOT NULL
    AND p."application_number" <> ''
) pub
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
  ON cd."symbol" = pub."first_cpc"
WHERE cd."level" = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Demonstrate an exponential moving average (EMA) with smoothing factor 0.2 for one CPC code.
WITH per_year AS (
  SELECT
    cd."symbol"                                  AS "cpc_symbol",
    YEAR(TO_DATE("filing_date"::STRING, 'YYYYMMDD')) AS "year",
    COUNT(*)                                     AS "yearly_count"
  FROM (
    SELECT 
      p."filing_date",
      f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS "first_cpc"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
    WHERE f."index" = 0
      AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
      AND p."filing_date" > 0
      AND p."application_number" IS NOT NULL
      AND p."application_number" <> ''
  ) pub
  JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
    ON cd."symbol" = pub."first_cpc"
  WHERE cd."level" = 5
    AND cd."symbol" = 'H04L29/08'  -- example CPC; replace as needed
  GROUP BY 1,2
)
SELECT
  "cpc_symbol",
  "year",
  "yearly_count",
  -- Exponential moving average using Snowflake's window functions
  ROUND(
    SUM("yearly_count" * POWER(1 - 0.2, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year") - 1))
    OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year"
          ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)
    /
    SUM(POWER(1 - 0.2, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year") - 1))
    OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year"
          ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)
  ,2) AS "ema_0_2"
FROM per_year
ORDER BY "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Sketch of selecting, for each CPC level‑5 group, the “best year” with the highest EMA (smoothing factor 0.2).
WITH year_counts AS (
  SELECT
    cd."symbol"                                  AS "cpc_symbol",
    cd."titleFull"                               AS "cpc_title",
    YEAR(TO_DATE("filing_date"::STRING, 'YYYYMMDD')) AS "year",
    COUNT(*)                                     AS "yearly_count"
  FROM (
    SELECT 
      p."filing_date",
      f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS "first_cpc"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
    WHERE f."index" = 0
      AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
      AND p."filing_date" > 0
      AND p."application_number" IS NOT NULL
      AND p."application_number" <> ''
  ) pub
  JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
    ON cd."symbol" = pub."first_cpc"
  WHERE cd."level" = 5
  GROUP BY 1,2,3
), ema_calc AS (
  SELECT
    "cpc_symbol",
    "cpc_title",
    "year",
    "yearly_count",
    -- EMA numerator and denominator calculated separately
    SUM("yearly_count" * POWER(1 - 0.2, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year") - 1))
      OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year" 
            ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) /
    SUM(POWER(1 - 0.2, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year") - 1))
      OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "year" 
            ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)  AS "ema_0_2"
  FROM year_counts
)
SELECT
  "cpc_symbol",
  "cpc_title",
  "year"             AS "best_year",
  ROUND("ema_0_2",2) AS "max_ema"
FROM (
  SELECT *,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "cpc_symbol" ORDER BY "ema_0_2" DESC) AS rn
  FROM ema_calc
)
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

